1
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:20,650
Well done, little genius.

2
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:23,080
Can we talk for a moment...?

3
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:28,960
What do you want? Make it short.

4
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:30,800
Okay, okay.

5
00:00:31,770 --> 00:00:37,140
...Our star Sendou got into another fight with that violent accessory you brought along.

6
00:00:37,390 --> 00:00:39,750
...And I doubt the two of them will ever get along.

7
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:40,720
Like I care.

8
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:44,310
...Then just kick that trash star off the team.

9
00:00:44,310 --> 00:00:51,380
...No... You may see him as trash... but to us, he's our star.

10
00:00:53,050 --> 00:00:59,260
...That's why a large number of our players say they won't play the match if Sendou is removed from the team.

11
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:04,500
...And in this way, the withdrawals will snowball and the players will boycott the match.

12
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:08,360
After hearing this, are you still sticking to your opinion... little genius...?

13
00:01:09,510 --> 00:01:10,750
Are you threatening me...?

14
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:11,880
...Not at all.

15
00:01:12,150 --> 00:01:15,580
...I don't think anyone wants the match to be cancelled.

16
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:20,550
...This is just my sympathy for you, being treated as a material to attract the crowd.

17
00:01:21,990 --> 00:01:23,560
So what do you want?

18
00:01:23,850 --> 00:01:26,670
Lead us to victory without using Shidou.

19
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:30,430
That should be very easy for a genius like you, right?

20
00:01:31,590 --> 00:01:33,790
Is this the team's wish?

21
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:37,580
Or did those old geezers at the JFU tell you to say this?

22
00:01:38,570 --> 00:01:49,290
...Well... 99% of this is my selfish desire to know what you can do for our current team.

23
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:54,640
...The remaining 1% is my duty as the captain, I guess.

24
00:01:55,030 --> 00:01:58,220
I also can't stand those money-hungry old dogs.

25
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:02,060
...What a selfish captain you are.

26
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:07,060
...Interesting... I'll play along with your provocation.

27
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:10,650
Huh? Thanks! You've got a nice side, contrary to what I expected.

28
00:02:15,230 --> 00:02:16,930
Don't get the wrong idea.

29
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:19,700
I'm the one testing you, not the other way around.

30
00:02:20,030 --> 00:02:23,360
And if you can't keep up with me, I'll leave the match immediately.

31
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:26,340
Understood, understood.

32
00:02:26,910 --> 00:02:28,380
...As you wish.

33
00:02:29,590 --> 00:02:31,040
Little genius.

34
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:31,950
...That day... strangely, I was calm.

35
00:04:41,470 --> 00:04:45,260
...I didn't care about anything except what I had to do.

36
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:48,280
...I wasn't worried about who I'd play against or which stadium I'd play in.

37
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:17,670
...What helped me think this way were the fifteen days of training prior.

38
00:05:22,210 --> 00:05:26,760
...And probably the reason for the training's success was the clarity of our goal and our strong drive to achieve it.

39
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:37,840
How can we focus intensely on this challenge that will ignite our spirits...?

40
00:05:42,110 --> 00:05:44,250
...The answer to that lies in...

41
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:54,050
There's a football match today!

42
00:05:54,050 --> 00:05:56,490
Who are we playing against?

43
00:05:56,490 --> 00:05:58,780
Blue Lock...?

44
00:05:58,780 --> 00:06:00,840
...Never heard of them.

45
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:04,880
We're talking about the U-20 generation called the "Jewels of a Generation", plus Itoshi Sae!

46
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:06,380
It's nearly impossible for them to lose!

47
00:06:06,380 --> 00:06:09,890
But seriously...! I never expected Itoshi Sae to participate!

48
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:35,290
Please let me play football my own way.

49
00:06:35,290 --> 00:06:37,920
No! You must stick to the plan!

50
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:40,630
...Use the physique you've been blessed with!

51
00:06:40,630 --> 00:06:43,430
...And focus on holding the ball for the team!

52
00:06:48,410 --> 00:06:50,140
...Okay, okay.

53
00:06:55,140 --> 00:06:57,770
...Blue Lock... so it is.

54
00:07:36,090 --> 00:07:37,350
Do you want to come with me?

55
00:07:40,490 --> 00:07:41,210
Yes!

56
00:07:43,690 --> 00:07:45,350
Go! Go!

57
00:07:45,350 --> 00:07:46,400
Well done!

58
00:08:22,810 --> 00:08:25,400
This stadium is huge! I didn't know there was something like this here.

59
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:27,520
We'll be able to see Sae-kun in person!

60
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:28,580
I'll take the picture!

61
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:30,720
They're known as the "Jewels of a Generation"!

62
00:08:28,580 --> 00:08:29,610
Yay!

63
00:08:29,610 --> 00:08:32,490
Look at that huge Sendou poster! Look, look!

64
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:34,470
Japan U-20 has no weaknesses! Victory is almost guaranteed!

65
00:08:32,490 --> 00:08:36,490
I can't believe I'm going to watch Itoshi Sae's first match in the national team jersey!

66
00:08:34,470 --> 00:08:36,490
The Japan team led by Hoichi is heading onto the pitch!

67
00:08:36,490 --> 00:08:37,600
Bear!

68
00:08:36,490 --> 00:08:38,200
This is an extraordinary event!

69
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:40,910
Order number 120!

70
00:08:41,190 --> 00:08:42,620
Smile!

71
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:43,840
What a long queue!

72
00:08:43,290 --> 00:08:44,660
This way, please!

73
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:45,330
What's it like inside, I wonder?

74
00:08:45,660 --> 00:08:47,830
Take a picture of me next!

75
00:08:49,210 --> 00:08:51,990
All Itoshi Sae towels are sold out!

76
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:54,170
Seriously...?

77
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:56,140
What exactly is this...?

78
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:57,780
A bear...?

79
00:08:57,780 --> 00:08:59,770
What do you think, want one?

80
00:08:59,770 --> 00:09:01,220
No!

81
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:07,230
...There's one thing Japanese football needs to become the best in the world.

82
00:09:07,650 --> 00:09:10,600
And that is the birth of a revolutionary forward.

83
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:13,780
And based on my arbitrary and biased decisions,

84
00:09:13,410 --> 00:09:16,030
Hey! You're drinking already...?

85
00:09:13,780 --> 00:09:17,810
...I selected 300 forwards under the age of 18 from across Japan.

86
00:09:17,810 --> 00:09:21,610
And I've started an experiment to turn one of them into the world's best forward.

87
00:09:22,450 --> 00:09:25,250
...And that is the purpose of building this facility.

88
00:09:22,450 --> 00:09:25,690
Who's this smug glasses guy with the round head?

89
00:09:25,250 --> 00:09:26,950
Blue Lock.

90
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:26,950
...How should I know.

91
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:36,350
Look at this crowd, darling!

92
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:37,510
...Yeah!

93
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:41,560
Is Yoichi really going to play on this pitch...?

94
00:09:43,370 --> 00:09:45,770
...It's indisputable how talented Itoshi Sae is, but...

95
00:09:45,770 --> 00:09:49,020
But defender Oliver Aiku is just as talented!

96
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:51,010
Really...?

97
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:55,740
Sae-kun is a world-class player, so he's on another level.

98
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:59,180
I traveled to Spain just to watch him play.

99
00:09:59,180 --> 00:10:01,330
Wow! You're so knowledgeable!

100
00:10:01,330 --> 00:10:03,890
So shall we open this champagne now...?

101
00:10:03,890 --> 00:10:07,720
...Well... Their opponents are just a bunch of failed high school students.

102
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:10,960
...So I think he'll score a hat-trick and the team will win like 5-0.

103
00:10:13,710 --> 00:10:14,890
Here, here!

104
00:10:14,890 --> 00:10:17,600
Wow! We're so close to the pitch!

105
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:32,030
You're so cool, Sendou-kun!!

106
00:10:32,030 --> 00:10:33,770
Aikuuuuu!

107
00:10:48,150 --> 00:10:49,120
...It's beginning!

108
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:54,270
Look at my jersey, Isagi! Does it suit me?

109
00:10:54,270 --> 00:10:55,880
Oh...! I think so!

110
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:59,590
This is the first time we're wearing our official Blue Lock uniforms, right?

111
00:10:59,590 --> 00:11:01,930
Yeah...! It makes you feel like your time has finally come!

112
00:11:02,390 --> 00:11:05,110
...We're really going to play against the U-20 National Team!

113
00:11:05,710 --> 00:11:07,890
We've come a long way to get here!

114
00:11:08,190 --> 00:11:10,100
But today's match isn't the end.

115
00:11:10,750 --> 00:11:12,850
This is our beginning... right?

116
00:11:13,750 --> 00:11:14,460
Right.

117
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:18,960
Alright, apologies for being late.

118
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:21,990
...I was undecided until the last minute, but...

119
00:11:23,940 --> 00:11:26,660
...These are the ones who will occupy the bench.

120
00:11:27,170 --> 00:11:28,910
We're only allowed three substitutions.

121
00:11:29,250 --> 00:11:34,960
So keep your composure and be ready to enter the match at any time.

122
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:37,430
...I've been put... on the bench.

123
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,980
...And this is our opponent's formation.

124
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:43,570
Shidou isn't in the lineup?

125
00:11:43,570 --> 00:11:46,280
Why?! Are they mocking us?

126
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:49,020
Maybe he didn't get along with them either?

127
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:51,250
Yeah, I bet it's something like that.

128
00:11:51,870 --> 00:11:53,230
But don't let it bother you.

129
00:11:53,620 --> 00:11:56,560
Because no matter what happens, your goal won't change.

130
00:11:57,710 --> 00:11:59,650
Execute the plan.

131
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:03,060
Listen up, you unpolished gems.

132
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:05,900
...The world doesn't know you exist yet.

133
00:12:07,170 --> 00:12:09,900
Don't you think this is the perfect stage to introduce yourselves?

134
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:13,750
...Change your fate in those ninety minutes.

135
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:18,670
And today, carve your egoism into the world.

136
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:22,260
We're the ones who will win today... Team Blue Lock!

137
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:23,320
Yessss!

138
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:24,410
Alright!

139
00:12:24,410 --> 00:12:25,170
Understood.

140
00:12:26,740 --> 00:12:28,050
...And now, let's go.

141
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:30,710
To our decisive battle!

142
00:12:41,190 --> 00:12:43,360
Here come the Blue Lock players!

143
00:12:44,410 --> 00:12:45,790
...Everyone's here.

144
00:12:45,790 --> 00:12:49,680
...So these... are the Japan U-20 National Team players.

145
00:13:09,870 --> 00:13:12,470
...And that's... Itoshi Sae.

146
00:13:13,350 --> 00:13:14,960
...Even I'm getting hyped about this!

147
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:17,560
...Yeah, I agree.

148
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:19,990
...I love this atmosphere!

149
00:13:19,990 --> 00:13:21,900
...I'm getting glamorously goosebumped!

150
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:24,670
You're the goalkeeper?

151
00:13:25,740 --> 00:13:28,770
I'm playing as a goalkeeper for the first time in my life today.

152
00:13:31,610 --> 00:13:35,120
That guy called Shidou, he was your teammate, right?

153
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:39,030
Sorry, but he won't set foot on this pitch today.

154
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:43,760
...We'll finish you off with a clean sheet, so good luck... Team Blue Lock.

155
00:13:44,890 --> 00:13:45,710
...Ah.

156
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:54,170
...If we lose today, it's the end of our football careers.

157
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:57,810
...I've survived moments like this before.

158
00:13:58,320 --> 00:14:01,030
...That's what landed me on this pitch today.

159
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,570
Japan!

160
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:05,320
Japan!

161
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:06,800
Japan!

162
00:14:07,530 --> 00:14:08,870
Japan!

163
00:14:09,450 --> 00:14:10,450
Japan!

164
00:14:10,950 --> 00:14:12,110
Japan!

165
00:14:12,770 --> 00:14:14,020
Japan!

166
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:15,790
Japan!

167
00:14:16,170 --> 00:14:17,170
Japan!

168
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:19,260
Japan!

169
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:20,740
Japan!

170
00:14:21,420 --> 00:14:22,510
Japan!

171
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:24,330
Japan!

172
00:14:24,850 --> 00:14:25,840
Japan!

173
00:14:26,510 --> 00:14:27,600
Japan!

174
00:14:28,350 --> 00:14:29,390
Japan!

175
00:14:30,060 --> 00:14:31,140
Japan!

176
00:14:31,730 --> 00:14:56,870
Japan! Japan! Japan! Japan! Japan!

177
00:14:54,070 --> 00:14:55,390
......Incredible.

178
00:14:57,320 --> 00:15:00,080
The match the people of Japan have been eagerly anticipating is about to begin!

179
00:15:00,420 --> 00:15:02,320
And the stadium is packed to the brim!

180
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:04,130
What do you think about this, Natsuki-san?

181
00:15:04,130 --> 00:15:06,930
What can I say other than this is the most amazing atmosphere?

182
00:15:06,930 --> 00:15:08,750
I can't believe my eyes!

183
00:15:08,750 --> 00:15:12,260
But no wonder! Itoshi Sae himself is playing in today's match!

184
00:15:12,260 --> 00:15:14,540
That's why the whole world is watching it!

185
00:15:14,540 --> 00:15:15,790
You're right!

186
00:15:16,220 --> 00:15:19,250
And now, here are the lineups for both teams!

187
00:15:19,250 --> 00:15:22,230
And as expected, the star player Itoshi Sae is playing in the attacking midfield position!

188
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:25,440
...This match, broadcast live from Blue Lock's main stadium,

189
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:27,580
...will kick off in just a few moments!

190
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:33,750
...I guess I've really... come much further than I ever imagined.

191
00:15:35,170 --> 00:15:40,060
...I never could have pictured the scene before me now before I came to Blue Lock.

192
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:47,470
I wonder how far I can go in front of this massive crowd...?

193
00:15:50,170 --> 00:15:52,050
...No...! That's wrong thinking.

194
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:55,710
...I shouldn't care about what's happening around me at all.

195
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:01,850
...I just need to... focus on myself.

196
00:16:03,010 --> 00:16:05,190
...And completely immerse myself in this match!

197
00:16:07,260 --> 00:16:08,400
How pathetic.

198
00:16:09,020 --> 00:16:11,610
What are you afraid of, you idiot?

199
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,930
On the contrary, I'm pumped, moron.

200
00:16:15,330 --> 00:16:38,890
Japan! Japan! Japan! Japan! Japan!

201
00:16:30,870 --> 00:16:32,590
Let's go, Isagi!

202
00:16:33,130 --> 00:16:33,840
Right!

203
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:38,440
...I will change... the world with my goals!

204
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:44,980
It's kickoff time... Team Blue Lock!

205
00:16:48,860 --> 00:16:52,010
...Our offensive method is built around me, Rin...

206
00:16:54,790 --> 00:16:56,020
...and Nagi.

207
00:16:56,950 --> 00:16:59,330
...We three will build up the play.

208
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:03,880
...And everything will be built upon this triangle!

209
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:10,740
...The foundation of the 4-5-1 formation is revolving around the center forward Itoshi Rin.

210
00:17:11,580 --> 00:17:14,300
...But that's only when we're defending.

211
00:17:14,630 --> 00:17:19,430
...When we attack, the team's beating heart, Karasu Tabito, will drop back slightly.

212
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:24,680
...And defend as a third center back.

213
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:25,960
...Understood.

214
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:30,170
...And the full-backs will advance into midfield.

215
00:17:30,170 --> 00:17:35,740
Transforming the formation into a 3-6-1, a deadly offensive formation relying on packing the midfield.

216
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:40,070
...And this flexible formation that enables scoring from anywhere

217
00:17:40,070 --> 00:17:43,450
became possible thanks to the entire team consisting of forwards.

218
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:48,040
This is Blue Lock's deadly offensive formation!

219
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:50,250
...They've packed the midfield.

220
00:17:52,270 --> 00:17:55,970
...We must not miss this moment while they haven't adapted to us yet!

221
00:17:56,610 --> 00:17:57,640
...Go!

222
00:17:58,220 --> 00:17:59,430
You monster!

223
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:02,240
...Time to get going!

224
00:18:03,640 --> 00:18:06,310
Hold on, little one, are you planning to pass through here?

225
00:18:06,610 --> 00:18:08,230
Got a problem with that?

226
00:18:09,660 --> 00:18:10,650
...He's fast!

227
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:13,570
...From the double touch feint... he's going through here!

228
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:20,030
He's maintaining his top speed... while turning with the ball...?

229
00:18:20,580 --> 00:18:21,780
Here I go!

230
00:18:22,130 --> 00:18:23,620
The spinning aerial charge!

231
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:29,540
...And now, next...! A quick pass into the penalty area!

232
00:18:30,130 --> 00:18:30,920
...No.

233
00:18:31,150 --> 00:18:32,420
...Not there either.

234
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:36,010
...The only one who resonates with my ideal vision is...

235
00:18:38,270 --> 00:18:40,590
Just as I expected, it's you, Isagi!

236
00:18:41,080 --> 00:18:43,150
...I love you so much, my partner!

237
00:18:43,150 --> 00:18:45,980
...Let's destroy them both.

238
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:49,480
...The U-20 National Team and everyone in this stadium!

239
00:18:51,750 --> 00:18:53,090
...I slipped behind them.

240
00:18:53,090 --> 00:18:54,830
...You're amazing, Bachira!

241
00:18:55,290 --> 00:18:58,050
...I trust your dribbling more than anyone!

242
00:18:58,730 --> 00:18:59,740
...I can do this.

243
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,740
...Our style of football.

244
00:19:02,340 --> 00:19:04,160
It works against them too!

245
00:19:11,780 --> 00:19:12,550
...What?

246
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:14,500
No way...?

247
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:16,660
What brought him here...?

248
00:19:17,460 --> 00:19:20,430
Impossible...! He managed to reach it...?

249
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:29,450
What an incredible clearance from Oliver Aiku!!!

250
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:31,560
What just happened...?

251
00:19:32,510 --> 00:19:34,950
Prediction...?! Or maybe just a reflex...?

252
00:19:34,950 --> 00:19:37,690
No, wait, maybe... it's both...?

253
00:19:38,310 --> 00:19:42,850
...Players' positions... my speed... the spot where the pass will land.

254
00:19:43,590 --> 00:19:49,140
...He grasped all of them in an instant... then moved relying on his reflexes!

255
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:53,980
...His field of vision... his intelligence... his physique.

256
00:19:54,560 --> 00:19:57,000
Just how many abilities does that bastard have...?

257
00:19:58,090 --> 00:20:07,700
Aiku! Aiku! Aiku! Aiku! Aiku! Aiku! Aiku!

258
00:19:58,100 --> 00:20:04,090
...So this is the U-20 National Team's defender and captain... Oliver Aiku.

259
00:20:06,110 --> 00:20:09,220
...You know, Blue Lock player number 11.

260
00:20:10,190 --> 00:20:15,310
...People usually compare forwards to thieves... and defenders to cops.

261
00:20:16,460 --> 00:20:18,400
...So, over my dead body, I'm letting you

262
00:20:19,690 --> 00:20:23,490
steal goals right in front of me, you little thief.

263
00:20:23,490 --> 00:20:38,190
Aiku! Aiku! Aiku! Aiku! Aiku! Aiku! Aiku!

264
00:20:26,810 --> 00:20:31,080
...Even though Bachira and I gave it our best... he stopped us in the blink of an eye.

265
00:20:38,190 --> 00:20:42,470
Is the U-20 National Team this strong...?

266
00:20:43,660 --> 00:20:46,370
...Great...! I've finally found him.

267
00:20:47,130 --> 00:20:49,180
...The person I want to challenge!

268
00:20:50,320 --> 00:20:53,650
...He will be the wall that guides me to my flow!

269
00:20:55,510 --> 00:20:58,110
Then let me see you try, Mr. Policeman.

270
00:20:58,690 --> 00:21:01,000
You might want to handcuff me.

271
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:04,400
...Okay, okay.

272
00:22:36,790 --> 00:22:39,470
Blue Lock: Additional Time!

273
00:22:40,370 --> 00:22:42,520
Check this out, Nagi-kun.

274
00:22:43,550 --> 00:22:44,460
What's this, Yuki?

275
00:22:45,630 --> 00:22:50,320
It's the lineup of the U-20 National Team we're facing.

276
00:22:51,510 --> 00:22:52,800
I've never seen any of them before!

277
00:22:53,140 --> 00:22:55,950
Let's get some info on them to prepare for the match.

278
00:22:56,700 --> 00:22:59,610
This is their star forward, Sendou Shuto.

279
00:22:59,610 --> 00:23:02,270
He's already a starter and a scorer in the J1 League.

280
00:23:02,270 --> 00:23:04,670
According to this, both his shot and speed are top-notch.

281
00:23:06,070 --> 00:23:08,530
...But doesn't he kind of look like...

282
00:23:08,860 --> 00:23:10,900
...manga villains?

283
00:23:11,700 --> 00:23:13,370
I think I agree!

284
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:17,040
So what do you think about this guy Kitsunezato?

285
00:23:17,040 --> 00:23:18,090
Looks like a lemur!

286
00:23:18,090 --> 00:23:19,910
...He's actually a bit cute.

287
00:23:20,850 --> 00:23:24,170
And Neru reminds me of a hamster.

288
00:23:25,200 --> 00:23:28,130
...And this one looks like a sleep-deprived raccoon.

289
00:23:29,940 --> 00:23:31,100
...As for this one.

290
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:33,480
He looks like a weird kokeshi doll.

291
00:23:34,140 --> 00:23:35,790
...You didn't even compare him to an animal.

292
00:23:35,790 --> 00:23:38,310
Hey, you two! Keep it down!

293
00:23:39,480 --> 00:23:40,190
Rin-kun!

294
00:23:40,190 --> 00:23:42,940
Are you playing that stupid game again?

295
00:23:48,740 --> 00:23:51,820
Let's just cut it short and say they're all water flea droppings.

296
00:23:52,910 --> 00:23:54,430
Do water fleas even poop...?

297
00:23:55,660 --> 00:23:56,370
...So.

298
00:23:57,260 --> 00:23:58,370
What about him?

299
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:06,080
...A mosquito, I guess.

300
00:24:06,080 --> 00:24:09,520
A mosquito that buzzes annoyingly when I'm trying to sleep!!!

301
00:24:09,520 --> 00:24:14,380
...A mosquito with an annoying, rude personality that you try to surpass but can't beat!

302
00:24:14,730 --> 00:24:18,220
It's a detestable, worthless creature just like him!

303
00:24:18,580 --> 00:24:22,580
...Disgusting... how disgusting... and how weak you are.

304
00:24:24,610 --> 00:24:27,630
Let's kill Itoshi Sae and get rid of him!

305
00:24:27,630 --> 00:24:30,190
Let's not play this game again, okay...?